N-2a-2 (the Nocturne audio backend, docs/NOCTURNE.md section 6.5) --
register the thylacine audio driver in SDL's compile-time bootstrap
list, mirroring the 0001 video-bootstrap patch. Two hunks against the
pristine vendored tree:

  - SDL_sysaudio.h: the THYLACINEAUDIO_bootstrap extern.
  - SDL_audio.c: the #ifdef'd bootstrap array entry, placed just ahead
    of DUMMYAUDIO so SDL_AudioInit picks thylacine first when the driver
    makes itself available (its Init probes /srv/nocturne and returns
    FALSE on a soundless machine; DUMMY then wins there only because patch
    0003 makes it auto-selectable -- upstream keeps it demand-only, which
    the auto-selection loop skips). Every other
    entry is #ifdef'd out on this target, so ahead-of-DUMMY is ahead of
    all.

The driver itself lives OUTSIDE the vendored tree at
usr/ports/sdl2/thylacine/SDL_thylacineaudio.{c,h}, staged by build_sdl2
into src/audio/thylacine/.

--- a/src/audio/SDL_sysaudio.h
+++ b/src/audio/SDL_sysaudio.h
@@ -198,5 +198,6 @@
 extern AudioBootStrap HAIKUAUDIO_bootstrap;
 extern AudioBootStrap COREAUDIO_bootstrap;
 extern AudioBootStrap DISKAUDIO_bootstrap;
+extern AudioBootStrap THYLACINEAUDIO_bootstrap;
 extern AudioBootStrap DUMMYAUDIO_bootstrap;
 extern AudioBootStrap FUSIONSOUND_bootstrap;
--- a/src/audio/SDL_audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/SDL_audio.c
@@ -132,6 +132,9 @@
 #ifdef SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_DISK
     &DISKAUDIO_bootstrap,
 #endif
+#ifdef SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_THYLACINE
+    &THYLACINEAUDIO_bootstrap,
+#endif
 #ifdef SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_DUMMY
     &DUMMYAUDIO_bootstrap,
 #endif
